Z||000000||Fret Naught||09-14-2000||03:10 PM||||I figured I better post this again, I had my car in for some body work, and the shop took the hood off. They did not mark the hinges, and the alignment is off. I am done dealing with those folks its the third time I had to take the car back. Does any one know of a set proceedure for aligning the hood? I messed with it for a couple of hours the other day, and just got totally frustrated.<P>Thanks in advance||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||09-14-2000||10:32 PM||||there's no procedure I know of. It's generally annoying as hell no matter what car it is. It's less annoying if you have help. You can make finer adjustments if someone is there to help hold it still while you tighten the bolts.||||reg||1
Z||000002||whamel||09-15-2000||11:19 AM||||I set the alignment on my hood when I took it off to do the radiator last weekend.  It was really a matter of having a second person and trying a lot of stuff in my case.  Unfortunately, I now realize the the hood was always straight - it's the rest of the ^&*% car that's crooked!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  (If you've seen my car, you'll realize this is pretty true.)<BR>Now the hood actually latches when it shuts and holds tight.  I thought the hood latch was broken before!<BR>    Here's the process I used, maybe it will help you.  (Keep in mind, my headlight motors are locked so I had a little trouble with that.)  I held up the hood while my wife tightened the bolts back down.  Tried to test fit it and was off about an inch and a half on the passenger side.  (By off, I mean hanging over.)  It was a matter of just making slight changes on each side one at a time then test closing it again and seeing if that worked.  I connected the prop rod while adjusting - honestly in hindsight, I may have been better off without it at first.  There's probably a better way, but it got the job done!<BR>     As far as how to get to the bolts the easiest way I can think of - I had to open my headlight covers to get there.  While holding them open, I put my hand through the cover and worked it there.  I couldn't get enough room to get a good grip unless I was coming through this side.  My lights are locked up and won't go down, very restrictive.  For my case it also kept me from hitting my just replaced lights and breaking them.  ||||reg||1
